gne(){return"Game rules"},
gzc(){return"2 decks of 52 cards, with or without jokers (your choice in a private room).\n13 cards each. On your turn the draw is automatic, then you may lay down; there is never a discard.\n\nFirst meld: your play must contain a clean run of three from your hand (3 consecutive cards of the same suit, no joker) within a single meld. From that very turn, you may extend it (even with a joker), lay down other melds and rearrange the table.\n\nAfter that, each turn you can:\n- lay down runs (3 or more consecutive cards of the same suit; the Ace goes low or high, but never King-Ace-2);\n- lay down sets of three or four (3-4 cards of the same rank, all different suits);\n- freely rearrange the table, as long as everything is valid when you confirm your play.\n\nThe joker stands in for any card; it can be moved around the table, but never taken back into your hand.\n\nThe first player to empty their hand wins the round; the others score penalty points (cards 2-10: face value; face cards: 10; Aces: 11; joker: 50).\n\nThe game ends when a player reaches 100 points: the least penalized wins. In a \u201csingle-round game\u201d, the first round won ends the game. These options (jokers, points game or single-round game) are chosen when creating a private room.\n\nIn public games: jokers included, single-round game (one round only), 120 seconds per turn \u2014 the turn is skipped automatically when time runs out.\n\nStock exhausted: the round stops and everyone counts the points left in their hand."},
